WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.257 --> 00:00:02.090
JOANNA SMITH: AppSheet
empowers your company

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:04.220
to build apps that are
flexible and scalable

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:06.900
without engineering resources.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.260
It's clever, no code platform
is easy for any employee

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.960
to use while providing
visibility and security

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.830
to your IT department.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.040
Consider an example where
a team in your organization

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:17.790
needs a new tool.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.250
Your IT department
likely doesn't

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:22.160
have the time or resources
to evaluate new solutions

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:23.600
for a single team.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.120
Fortunately, AppSheet
combines administrative tools,

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:28.070
such as setting
controls on data access,

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.530
with day-to-day products
like Google Sheets.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.030
This means your
IT department can

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:33.680
set organization
wide limits which

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.140
employees can work
within while customizing

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.153
their own solutions.

00:00:38.153 --> 00:00:40.070
Let's take a look at how
a facility management

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:43.260
team was able to build
their own inventory system.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.152
Here, the team
uses pen and paper

00:00:45.152 --> 00:00:47.360
to inventory equipment
throughout multiple buildings,

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:50.690
later adding their
updates to a Google Sheet.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:53.630
The process is slow
and often inaccurate.

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:56.120
Some buildings need new or
additional pieces of equipment

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:59.310
while others may have extra
items unaccounted for.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:01.340
IT has received
requests to improve

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:03.740
the way these items are
tracked by developing a custom

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:04.678
application.

00:01:04.678 --> 00:01:07.220
But that effort is sitting in
a backlog behind other projects

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:08.870
with higher priority.

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.300
The team most familiar
with the inventory process

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.920
is the facility management team.

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.170
And they've decided to take
on this project themselves

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:18.410
by using AppSheet, a no
code development platform.

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.960
The current process requires
many users contributing

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.670
to a single Google Sheet.

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:24.710
This sheet contains
all of the assets

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:27.350
and their locations
across multiple buildings.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.570
To upgrade the sheet
into an application,

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:31.850
the team lead starts by
connecting the shared Google

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:33.450
Sheet to AppSheet.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.450
The spreadsheet will serve
as the source of data

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:37.520
for the new application.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:39.920
Behind the scenes,
AppSheet is automatically

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.050
detecting the types
of data connected,

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:44.480
establishing relationships
between data sources,

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:47.330
and building an app
interface that's easy to use.

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:49.820
With a few clicks, the
tables of buildings and items

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:50.900
have been connected.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:53.720
And AppSheet has generated
a functional prototype.

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:57.440
This prototype already contains
a map of the buildings, methods

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:00.770
for adding items and updating
the status of each one,

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:02.660
as well as intuitive
ways to see lists

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:04.660
of items organized by the
building in which they

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:06.560
are located.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.570
At this point, the
app creator can easily

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:11.090
install this application on
their mobile device, where

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:12.710
any future updates
made to the app

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:15.080
will be instantly reflected.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:17.720
And anytime the app is used,
updates are synced back

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:19.670
to the database for
the application,

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:23.030
in this case, the
connected Google Sheet.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:25.040
The team lead can
customize their new tool

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.710
by adding additional
features to their app.

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:30.020
For example, with a
few clicks, the team

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:32.390
adds a dashboard displaying
the real time status

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:34.205
of every piece of equipment.

00:02:34.205 --> 00:02:36.830
Now everyone who was carrying a
clipboard around the facilities

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:40.340
can check the dashboard from the
mobile app or their computer.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.910
To create this dashboard,
the team lead adds a view,

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:48.980
selects dashboard, and then
chooses what data to include.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:50.920
The team also adds
barcode scanning

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:53.090
to help users quickly
and accurately identify

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:55.160
different pieces of equipment.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:57.800
To enable barcode
and NFC tag scanning,

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:00.500
the team lead simply flips
a toggle option on a field

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:04.850
by field basis, depending on
the data that's been connected.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:08.240
Lastly, email workflows can be
created to automatically notify

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:10.580
team members when
inventory gets low

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.320
or if there are unused
items that could

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.870
be moved to another building.

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:18.560
This email workflow is enabled
by creating a new workflow,

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.900
specifying the type
of notification,

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.700
and customizing an
email template that

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.490
will be filled out with the
appropriate information based

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:26.810
on app content.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:29.130
This app is ready to
start using right away.

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:31.280
And it can be shared
with individuals or teams

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:33.200
similar to how
Google Doc is shared.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:36.590
And it can be updated as needed
based on future feedback.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:39.320
The team was able to build
their own solution, relieving IT

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:40.910
of this backlogged
project while still

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:42.650
maintaining control
of what's created

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:44.360
and how data is accessed.

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:47.000
For example, establishing a
policy so that app creators

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.030
can share their apps only with
other employees in their group.

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:51.410
Other policies
can control things

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:53.390
like how data is
accessed or what features

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:55.370
can be included in apps.

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:57.410
AppSheet's no code
development environment

00:03:57.410 --> 00:03:59.540
is what enables
solutions like this.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:01.040
Other teams in this
organization can

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.170
take advantage of the
platform in similar ways

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:05.510
to help manage projects,
coordinate field staff,

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.730
or automate internal operations.

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:10.580
Empowering a single team
to improve their daily work

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:12.380
while ensuring the
entire organization

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:14.450
operates with clear
boundaries is exactly

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:16.519
the sort of flexible and
collaborative solution

00:04:16.519 --> 00:04:18.679
that AppSheet was designed for.

00:04:18.679 --> 00:04:22.629
[MUSIC PLAYING]

